                        <div class="snip" title="">
                            The members of the World Bank along with the NPMU officials, visited the state of Madhya
                            Pradesh from September 4 &amp; 5, 2023 to know the status of activities being performed under
                            Atal Bhujal scheme. During the mission period, discussions were held with the Principal
                            Secretary, Water Resources Department, Government of Madhya Pradesh, CEO Niwadi Zila
                            parishad and the officials of SPMU, DPMU, DIP and line departments associated with the
                            implementation of Atal Jal .
                            The team visited two Gram Panchayats namely Kumaharra Khas and Bhamoura located in
                            Niwadi Block, District Niwadi, Madhya Pradesh. In both the GPs, discussions were held with
                            the community members, representatives of the Village Water and Sanitation Committees
                            and DIPs. Main emphasis of the discussion was to know the process being followed for
                            calculation of water budget &amp; updating the Water Security Plan consisting of the Demand
